Problem Statement: Design a Movie Ticket Booking System
Overview:
Design the core classes, interfaces, and low-level architecture for a movie ticket booking system (similar to BookMyShow or Fandango).
The system should allow users to browse movies, select a cinema, choose a showtime, and book specific seats.
Core Requirements:
Cities, Cinemas, & Screens: The system should support multiple cities. Each city has multiple cinemas, and each cinema has multiple screens (halls).
Movies & Shows: A cinema can run multiple shows for different movies simultaneously. A movie has standard attributes (title, language, genre, duration).
A show is a specific screening of a movie at a specific time on a specific screen.
Seat Selection & Pricing: Screens have a specific layout of seats.
Seats can be of different categories (e.g., Standard, Premium, VIP), and pricing should dynamically reflect the seat category.
Booking Process: Users should be able to select available seats for a show and initiate a booking.
Concurrency Handling (Crucial): The system must handle high concurrency.
Two users cannot book the same seat for the same show simultaneously.
When a user selects a seat and proceeds to payment, the seat must be temporarily locked (e.g., for 10 minutes).
If the payment fails or times out, the seat must become available again.

Out of Scope (Do not implement):
User authentication and profile management.
Actual payment gateway integration (assume a mock PaymentService exists).
Recommendation engines or notification systems.

